<Item XName="Note" UserName="Note" Type="Notes">
<Description>Example text with pretty printing</Description>
<LibName>Eagleware</LibName>
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=5&gt;&lt;U&gt;Multi-Channels Calibration using SystemVue M9703 FPGA Design Flow&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=5&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;This workspace is an example that uses SystemVue M9703 FPGA design flow to calibrate magnitude and phase of M9703&apos;s two channels. It works for both M9703A and M9703B. The instruments connection is shown in &quot;Design3 (Schematic)&quot; and you can connection all instruments accordingly. Then you can run the simulation from Step1 to Step5 to do software simulation, download calibration reference signal to M8190 AWG and calibrate M9703 8-channels digitizer. You can observe the calibration results from the three figures:&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;DF1_Design3_I1:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Time domain waveforms of reference channel and calibration channel&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;DF1_Design3_mag_factor3:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Magnitude ratio between reference channel and calibration channel&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;STRONG&gt;( Magnitude(IN1) / Magnitude(IN3) )&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;DF1_Design3_phase_factor3:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Phase difference between reference channel and calibration channel; unit: degree&amp;nbsp;&lt;STRONG&gt; ( Phase(IN1) - Phase(IN3)&amp;nbsp;)&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;In this example, the NCO generates the fixed 320MHz IF sine and cosine waveforms and the calibration reference waveform is for 100MHz bandwidth calibration. So this example can calibrate IN3 channel aligned to IN1 channel in frequency range 270MHz ~ 370MHz. The calibration reference waveform is generated in subent &quot;freq_sequence&quot;. For the other IF frequency and bandwidth, it can be implemented based on this example.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;The FPGA design for FPGA0 and FPGA1 of M9703 are the same, but we can configure different calibration FIR coefficients to their BlockRegisters. The diagram of FPGA design is shown in subnet &quot;M9703_FPGA0&quot;.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;It needs that this workspace is in a writable directory to download waveform to M8190. So if you installed this example wordspace in a read-only directory, you need save this workspace in a writable directory and then run the simulations step by step.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;FONT size=5&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Calibration&amp;nbsp;Instruction:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Step1:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;It&apos;s software simulaiton mode. Run simulaton and observe the magnitude ratio and phase difference, which should match what we set in S3 and S8 SineGen models.&amp;nbsp;We generate 330MHz sine waveform with S8 for IN1 channel and set its magnitude as 1.1*625mV and phase as 0 degree. We generate 330MHz sine waveform with S3 for IN3 channel and set its magnitude as 625mV and phase as&amp;nbsp;5 degree. &lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;So the expected simulation results are almost 1.1 in figure &quot;DF1_Design3_mag_factor3&quot; and almost&amp;nbsp;5 degree in figure &quot;DF1_Design3_phase_factor3&quot;&amp;nbsp;when we bypass calibration FIR filters for both IN1 and IN3 channels. Then it means our design can detect the difference of magnitude and phase for two channels correctly. The software simulation results should prove that our FXP design meets our expection. &lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;Then we can open &amp;nbsp;&quot;HDL Code Generator1&quot; to run the FPGA bit file generation flow. It will take about 2 hours to generate the FPGA programming file. A generated FPGA image folder&amp;nbsp;has been&amp;nbsp;placed in this example directory.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Step2:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;Run the simulation. It will download calibration reference waveform (sine waveforms sequence) to M8190 for measurement.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;Note: You have to launch M8190 Firmware before run this simulation, then SystemVue can connect with M8190 instrument. In addition, you should find the socket port number from the launched M8190 Firmware and fill the socket port number as parameter &quot;SecAddress&quot; of M8190 download model. For example, you may find &quot;&lt;SPAN lang=EN&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;SCPI Access (Socket): TCPIP0::localhost::60005::SOCKET&lt;/STRONG&gt;&quot; from&amp;nbsp;the launched M8190 Firmware, then you need set &quot;SecAddress&quot; of M8190 download model as 60005. Otherwise, when you run this simulation at Step2, SystemVue will post an error to tell that it can&apos;t connect with M8190 instrument.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Step3:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;In Design3 Schematic, open M9703CosimBus model&apos;s customUI and&amp;nbsp;input your own generated&amp;nbsp;FPGA Image folder path (or the pre-generated FPGA image&amp;nbsp;folder in the example directory)&amp;nbsp;and select your own connected M9703 address.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;Run the simulation. It will ask M9703 to capture raw IQ output from reference channel and calibration channel. Observe the three results figures for magnitude/phase difference and waveform of I path output. They will show the IQ imbalance before the calibration.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;After the simulation is over,&amp;nbsp; the equation of this example will extract the raw IQ data and calculate the coefficients of FIR compensation filter. It&amp;nbsp;will be&amp;nbsp;executed automatically in background.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Step4:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;Run the simulation. It will download a LFM (Linear Frequency Modulation) signal to M8190. The LFM signal will cover all frequency components of our bandwidth (270MHz ~ 370MHz). Then we can use the extracted compensation coefficients for the LFM signal to observe the calibration performance for the whole bandwidth.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Step5:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;Run the simulation. It will ask M9703 to capture&amp;nbsp;calibrated IQ output from reference channel and calibration channel. And the current input signal for M9703 is LFM signal. Observe the three results figures for magnitude/phase difference and waveforms of I path output. Now the magnitude/phase difference should be very small and the time domain waveforms of reference and calibration channels should match very well.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=center&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;U&gt;&lt;FONT size=5&gt;DDC HDL Code Generation using Xilinx Vivado HLS Tool&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;In this example design, the DDC is designed using Xilinx Vivado HLS tool. We provide the C source code and directive file in the example folder. So you can modify the C source code to generate HDL codes to support different bandwidth for multi-channels calibration. &lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;Under the multi-channels calibration&amp;nbsp;example directory &quot;Examples\Hardware Design\M9703_FDK\Multi_Channels_Calibration&quot;, the C source code files are placed in folder &quot;cali_ddc_HLS\C_SourceCode&quot;. The top level files are &quot;DownResample.cpp&quot; and &quot;DownResample.h&quot;. You can create a Vivado HLS project and add all files in&amp;nbsp;&quot;cali_ddc_HLS\C_SourceCode&quot; folder as &quot;Source&quot;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;set the top function as &quot;DownResample&quot;.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;The directive file is placed in folder &quot;cali_ddc_HLS\Directives&quot;. Use this directive file in your Vivado HLS project, then&amp;nbsp;you can&amp;nbsp;generate your own HDL codes.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;The pre-generated VHDL files are placed in folder &quot;cali_ddc_HLS\vhdl&quot; and the pre-generated FPGA programming files are placed in folder &quot;M9703_MultiCh_Cali&quot;. The VHDL files and FPGA programming files&amp;nbsp;are generated for default 3 stages halfband filters setting. The default target bandwidth for calibration is 100MHz. You can use the pre-generated VHDL files for HDL cosimulation in Step1 and use the pre-generated FPGA programming files for M9703A hardware cosimulation in Step3 and Step5 directly for the default setting.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;If you want to modify the DDC to different settings, you can open &quot;DownResample.h&quot; to adjust the number of HALFBANDSTAGENUM to change the halfband filters stages.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;When HALFBANDSTAGENUM =1, only one halfband filter is used, the sample rate of compensation filter is 800MHz and the target calibration bandwidth is 400MHz.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;When HALFBANDSTAGENUM =2,&amp;nbsp;two halfband filters&amp;nbsp;are used, the sample rate of compensation filter is 400MHz and the target calibration bandwidth is 200MHz.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;When HALFBANDSTAGENUM =3,&amp;nbsp;three halfband filters&amp;nbsp;are used, the sample rate of compensation filter is 200MHz and the target calibration bandwidth is 100MHz. (Default settings)&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;Then you can run &quot;Synthesis&quot; of your own created Vivado HLS project to generate HDL files. Then you can use HDL model of SystemVue to wrap up your generated HDL files as a model and do HDL cosimulation in M9703 Template design subnet to verify its function. After that, you can run the automatic FPGA programming file generation flow to get the final FPGA programming files to run with M9703 hardware.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;</Text>
